{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":349606,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"d2b15533-126e-4161-b515-589504b51580","total_cost_usd":1.1270395,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":38862,"cache_read_input_tokens":20629,"output_tokens":28085,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":38862,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":28085,"cache_read_input_tokens":20629,"cache_creation_input_tokens":38862,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":38862},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":25865,"outputTokens":21,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.02597,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":28085,"cacheReadInputTokens":20629,"cacheCreationInputTokens":38862,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.1010695,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\n  \"agent\": \"economy-balancer\",\n  \"flight\": {\n    \"dry_mass_kg\": 650,\n    \"fuel_capacity_kg\": 420,\n    \"thrust_n\": 28500,\n    \"fuel_burn_kgs\": 6.5,\n    \"rcs_thrust_n\": 1200,\n    \"rcs_fuel_burn_kgs\": 0.4,\n    \"rotation_rate_degs\": 90\n  },\n  \"cargo\": {\n    \"base_slots\": 7,\n    \"compactor_tier\": 1\n  },\n  \"reentry\": {\n    \"heat_capacity\": 208,\n    \"heat_dissipation_s\": 5,\n    \"cargo_damage_interval_s\": 3,\n    \"unstaged_heat_multiplier\": 3.0,\n    \"off_retrograde_penalty\": 1.0,\n    \"commit_floor_m\": 8000\n  },\n  \"ablation\": {\n    \"cycle_toll_base_pct\": 8.0,\n    \"cycle_toll_growth\": 1.75,\n    \"heat_cost_coefficient\": 0.0009,\n    \"heat_cost_exponent\": 2.0,\n    \"skim_peak\": 52,\n    \"skim_heat_multiplier\": [1.0, 0.48, 0.45, 0.44],\n    \"heat_index\": { \"bottom\": 100.0, \"middle\": 116.7, \"top\": 144.7 },\n    \"cost_curve\": {\n      \"bottom\": [17.0, 26.51, 53.19, 98.42],\n      \"middle\": [20.26, 27.26, 53.85, 99.05],\n      \"top\": [26.84, 28.78, 55.18, 100.32]\n    },\n    \"plate_capacity_pct\": 100,\n    \"optimal_skims\": { \"bottom\": 0, \"middle\": 0, \"top\": 0 }\n  },\n  \"landing\": {\n    \"soft_landing_ms\": 5.0,\n    \"damage_per_ms_over\": 6.0,\n    \"no_gear_multiplier\": 2.0,\n    \"fragile_multiplier\": 2.0,\n    \"parachute_area_m2\": 480,\n    \"parachute_drag_coefficient\": 1.8,\n    \"descent_speed_full_hold_ms\": 4.4\n  },\n  \"tow_fee\": {\n    \"free_radius_m\": 1200,\n    \"max_fee_fraction\": 0.5,\n    \"curve\": \"linear\"\n  },\n  \"eva\": {\n    \"suit_mass_kg\": 110,\n    \"jetpack_thrust_n\": 240,\n    \"jetpack_fuel_kg\": 18,\n    \"jetpack_burn_kgs\": 0.35,\n    \"base_tether_slots\": 2,\n    \"magnet_hold_force_n\": 900,\n    \"magnet_range_screens\": 0.125,\n    \"latch_jerk_coefficient\": 1.0,\n    \"swing_jerk_coefficient\": 1.0\n  },\n  \"economy\": {\n    \"launch_cost\": 120,\n    \"replate_cost_per_pct\": 3,\n    \"repair_cost_per_pct\": 5,\n    \"value_gradient\": { \"at_bottom\": 1.0, \"at_top\": 5.5 },\n    \"size_class_base_value\": { \"small\": 40, \"medium\": 90, \"oversized\": 320 },\n    \"fragile_value_premium\": 3.0\n  },\n  \"upgrades\": [\n    { \"part\": \"hand_magnet\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 680, \"effect\": \"magnet_range_screens\", \"value\": 0.1875 },\n    { \"part\": \"fuel_tank\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 750, \"effect\": \"fuel_capacity_kg\", \"value\": 560 },\n    { \"part\": \"thruster\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 850, \"effect\": \"thrust_n\", \"value\": 33000 },\n    { \"part\": \"parachute\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 1000, \"effect\": \"parachute_area_m2\", \"value\": 700 },\n    { \"part\": \"storage\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 1100, \"effect\": \"base_slots\", \"value\": 10 },\n    { \"part\": \"heat_shield\", \"tier\": 1, \"cost\": 1250, \"effect\": \"heat_capacity\", \"value\": 222 },\n    { \"part\": \"hand_magnet\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 1500, \"effect\": \"magnet_range_screens\", \"value\": 0.25 },\n    { \"part\": \"fuel_tank\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 1600, \"effect\": \"fuel_capacity_kg\", \"value\": 700 },\n    { \"part\": \"thruster\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 1900, \"effect\": \"thrust_n\", \"value\": 38000 },\n    { \"part\": \"parachute\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 2350, \"effect\": \"parachute_area_m2\", \"value\": 1200 },\n    { \"part\": \"storage\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 2500, \"effect\": \"base_slots\", \"value\": 13 },\n    { \"part\": \"heat_shield\", \"tier\": 2, \"cost\": 2950, \"effect\": \"heat_capacity\", \"value\": 238 }\n  ],\n  \"balance_notes\": [\n    \"Full-hold mass doubling (GDD 2.2, 2.5): dry_mass_kg is 650 kg — the staged mass that actually flies the descent and hangs under the canopy; the thruster and tank are gone by then and Armstrong rebuilds them per launch (2.5), so they are not in this number. base_slots is 7 and every piece is one slot (4.3 cut the size classes). Seven slots at the catalog's top-third ordinary mean of 106.1 kg is 742.7 kg of cargo, so a full hold lands at 650 + 742.7 = 1392.7 kg. That is 2.14x the dry mass — 'roughly doubles' — and it reproduces the GDD's flown full-hold figure of ~1,398 kg to within 0.4%. It also lands on the Researcher's ballistic coefficients exactly: staged empty 650 / (1.4 * 3.5) = 132.7 kg/m2, full hold 1392.7 / 4.9 = 284.2 kg/m2 against their stated 285, and the module at 650 + 3600 = 4250 gives 867 kg/m2, above their 'over 730'. Their warning that a staged dry mass under ~490 kg would drop beta below 100 is not triggered.\",\n    \"Commit floor and the four peaks (GDD 2.2): reentry.commit_floor_m = 8000. At that floor the Researcher's density ladder gives rho = 1.5 * exp(-8000/3100) = 0.1136 kg/m3, two decades below sea level — deep enough that a committed entry cannot be flown cool, shallow enough that the ship pulls out rather than lithobrakes. It sits 35,000 m below atmosphere_top_m, so it is a real constraint and not the no-op a floor near the interface would be, and it is 8 km above the ground rather than at zero, so an empty hold is not taxed into a dive. The four peaks it produces from the top of the band, in bar units: empty ship 144.7 plunge / 86.2 on one skim; full hold at base storage 203.7 / 125.5; Armstrong's module 268.8 / 196.5.\",\n    \"Heat capacity ladder (GDD 2.2, 2.5): the ladder is 208 base, 222 tier 1, 238 tier 2. Every tier clears the base-storage full hold's 203.7 plunge, so an empty ship and a full hold plunge freely from anywhere in the band at every tier. Every tier sits below the module's 268.8 plunge — the maxed tier by 11.5% — so no shield purchase buys the plunge back and the win condition keeps the mechanic it is built around. The module's skimmed peak of 196.5 is under the base capacity, so one braking pass brings it home at any tier. The binding lower bound on this ladder is the full hold's 203.7, not the module: base capacity clears it by only 2.1%, which is thin, and it is thin because the charter's own (196.5, 203.7] window is 4% wide. I did not try to widen it by forcing the full hold to skim. The climb's measured 47.5 bar units is 23% of the base capacity — a visible, safe first lesson, though a quieter one than the half-bar GDD 4.4 hoped for; the (203.7, 268.8) window leaves no room for a lower starter capacity, and this is the closest legal value.\",\n    \"Ablation optimum (charter method step 3): with cycle_toll_base_pct 8.0, cycle_toll_growth 1.75, heat_cost_coefficient 0.0009, heat_cost_exponent 2.0 and skim_peak 52, the emitted cost_curve minimises at k = 0 at all three samples — bottom 17.00 against 26.51, middle 20.26 against 27.26, top 26.84 against 28.78. That is the flown truth the charter states: with entry depth free the plunge is always the cheapest descent, and the design takes its multi-pass requirement from heat_capacity instead. Growth is 1.75, comfortably above 1, so the toll on cycle i is 8.0 * 1.75^i — 8.0, 14.0, 24.5, 42.9 — and three skims already burn 100.3% of plate at the top. A six-pass feathering descent costs 8.0 * (1.75^7 - 1) / 0.75 = 514% of plate in toll alone, so feathering is priced out rather than merely discouraged, which is what the charter asks given a skim costs 0 m/s of dv and about six minutes.\",\n    \"The module's finale is affordable but tight, which is the point: its skimmed descent is one skim plus one commit, so toll 8.0 + 14.0 = 22.0, plus 0.0009 * 196.5^2 = 34.75 for the committed entry, plus 0.0009 * 52^2 = 2.43 for the skim itself — 59.2% of plate. It comes home with 41% of the shield left and no margin for a second pass, and the plunge it cannot fly would have cost 0.0009 * 268.8^2 = 65.0 plus 8.0 toll even if the bar allowed it.\",\n    \"Parachute descent speed at full hold (GDD 2.3): parachute_area_m2 = 480 at parachute_drag_coefficient = 1.8. With the Researcher's planet, v = sqrt(2 * m * g / (rho_0 * Cd * A)) = sqrt(2 * 1392.7 * 9 / (1.5 * 1.8 * 480)) = sqrt(25068.6 / 1296.0) = sqrt(19.343) = 4.398 m/s, emitted as descent_speed_full_hold_ms = 4.4. That is under the 5.0 m/s soft line with 12% of margin, which is what makes the Parachute a real purchase and not a formality. This is a prediction the flight can contradict — the canopy is stated, not solved backwards out of the speed. Empty at 650 kg the same canopy gives 3.01 m/s.\",\n    \"Storage and Parachute as a pair (charter step 8): a maxed 13-slot hold at the top third carries 1379.3 kg, so a maxed-storage full hold lands at 770 + 1379.3 = 2149 kg on the base canopy — sqrt(38682 / 1296) = 5.46 m/s, over the line and a hard landing. Parachute tier 1 at 700 m2 pulls that to 4.52 m/s. The 770 kg is the maxed staged dry mass: 650 base, +250 for the two storage tiers, -180 for the two shield tiers (the only mass-reducing buy, GDD 2.5), +50 for the two canopies; the thruster and tank tiers add nothing because they are jettisoned. Parachute tier 2 at 1200 m2 exists for the finale: the module lands at 770 + 3600 = 4370 kg, sqrt(78660 / 3240) = 4.93 m/s — under 5.0 by 1.4%, so the pristine delivery requires the maxed canopy and a clean flare, and tier 1 would give 5.44 m/s and cost the module a state.\",\n    \"Break-even for a lazy run (GDD 2.5): launch_cost is 120. A crumpled panel stack at 56,000 m prices at small base 40 * (1.0 + 4.5 * 6000/230000) = 40 * 1.117 = 44.7, so the launch fee is 2.7 cheap pieces — the GDD's 'two to three' exactly. A lazy ballistic arc to the band floor never reaches orbital speed and comes back near the bottom sample's cheapest column, burning on the order of 6% of plate, so replating at 3 per percent adds ~18 and the turnaround is ~138. Four floor pieces — two panel stacks at 44.7 and two bent truss sections at 90 * (1.0 + 4.5 * 17000/230000) = 120 each — pay 329, so the lazy run clears its own turnaround roughly 2.4x. The mercy floor still applies: cash stopping at zero can never block a launch.\",\n    \"No shear under steady tow (charter step 6): steady towing tension is the towed mass times the achieved acceleration, a = jetpack_thrust_n / (suit_mass_kg + towed). The worst legal cases are two impact-pitted engine bells at 122 kg each — a = 240 / 354 = 0.678 m/s2, tension 244 * 0.678 = 165 N — and Armstrong's module at 3600 kg, a = 240 / 3710 = 0.065 m/s2, tension 3600 * 0.065 = 233 N. magnet_hold_force_n is 900, a 3.9x margin over the worst steady case, so shear can only ever fire on latch jerk or swing jerk, both left at coefficient 1.0. Towing two mid-band pieces (mean 52.9 kg each) drops bare-suit acceleration from 2.18 to 1.11 m/s2 — halved, noticeably heavier, still flyable.\",\n    \"Flight and the first launch (GDD 2.5, charter step 1): thrust_n 28500 at fuel_burn_kgs 6.5 is an exhaust velocity of 4385 m/s; launch mass is 650 staged + 110 stage structure + 420 fuel = 1180 kg, for a liftoff TWR of 2.68. Reaching the GDD's measured 56.2 km apex needs about 889 m/s of vertical energy (mu * (1/R - 1/r) = 3.6e11 * (1/200000 - 1/256200), v = sqrt(2 * 394848)) plus roughly 300 m/s of gravity loss over the 46 s burn and 80 m/s of drag — 1269 m/s, which is ln(1180/883) = 0.289 of the 1929 m/s the full tank carries. That leaves 29.4% of the tank at apex against the GDD's measured 29.5%. The 15.7 points of tank the GDD attributes to drag is inside the 80 m/s term. Circularisation margins at the floor, and whether fuel_tank tier 1's 560 kg delivers the GDD's 10.9%, are for the simulator to measure — I can defend the arc, not the gravity turn.\",\n    \"Upgrade pacing (charter step 8): twelve purchases total 18,430. Costs escalate 680 to 2,950 and the cheapest-first order is hand magnet, tank, thruster, parachute, storage, shield, then the same six at tier 2 — so Parachute tier 1 (1,000) is affordable before Storage tier 1 (1,100) and Parachute tier 2 (2,350) before Storage tier 2 (2,500), which keeps the counterweight ahead of the difficulty on the natural spending path. A mid-band run with 7 slots of medium wreckage at 150,000 m nets about 1,600 and a maxed top-band run about 5,800, so 13-15 runs clears the ladder with three to five learning failures losing their hauls — inside the GDD's 12-15, flexing to 18 as 2.5 allows, with no price moved.\",\n    \"Tow fee (charter step 5, GDD 2.5): free_radius_m 1200 is one screen of the pad, and the fee rises linearly to max_fee_fraction 0.5 at half the planet's circumference, pi * 200000 = 628,319 m — a slope of 8.0e-7 of haul value per metre beyond the free radius. It is a fraction of the haul, so it can never go negative, never exceed 50%, and never touch savings.\",\n    \"One thing I could not fix from here. The full-hold-doubling claim is only true against the top third of the catalog. Seven slots at the bottom third's 19.8 kg mean is 139 kg — 21% of dry mass, not 100% — so 'a full hold roughly doubles the ship' is a property of a top-of-band haul, not of the starter hop the charter points me at. The honest fix is either heavier low-band debris or a smaller base hold, and both are somewhere I cannot reach: the catalog belongs to the Debris Designer (concern filed) and base_slots is on screen in the GDD's own walkthrough. I set base_slots to 7 because that is what makes the reentry table's 1,398 kg and the Researcher's 285 kg/m2 come out right, and I am stating the floor-of-band shortfall rather than moving the thing being measured.\"\n  ],\n  \"catalog_concerns\": [\n    \"crumpled_panel_stack (and the whole bottom third), mass_kg: at 5.5-15.5 kg the floor population cannot make the GDD's full-hold-doubling rule true. Seven slots of it is 139 kg against a 650 kg dry mass. I balanced the doubling against the top third's 106.1 kg ordinary mean, which reproduces the GDD's flown 1,398 kg full hold, but that leaves the claim false everywhere below mid-band. Either the floor masses want raising by a factor of about five, or the rule wants restating as a top-of-band property.\",\n    \"collapsed_dish_frame, buckled_pressure_bulkhead, severed_boom_mast, size_class / hand_tetherable: all three are oversized and hand_tetherable false, and GDD 4.3 cut the crane magnet and the oversized class from scope. As the catalog stands these three pieces can never enter a hold, so the oversized entry in size_class_base_value (320) prices something unreachable. Either they want demoting to medium or the catalog wants them removed from the shipping slice.\",\n    \"armstrongs_module, spawn_weight: it carries spawn_weight 1, which places the win condition inside the ordinary weighted spawn pool. It is a fixed objective at a fixed altitude (GDD 2.6), not a roll, and any sampler that reads spawn_weight literally can hand it to the player on run one. It wants a flag that takes it out of the pool rather than a weight of 1.\",\n    \"size_classes block, slots_crushed / slots_uncrushed: the block still prices small at 1-2 slots, medium at 2-4 and oversized at 6-12, but GDD 4.3 cut size classes and states every piece is one slot. I balanced base_slots = 7 as seven pieces. If the slot table is live rather than vestigial, every mass figure in this file that depends on hold count is wrong by the crush factor.\"\n  ]\n}","ttft_ms":269947,"ttft_stream_ms":1629,"time_to_request_ms":193,"type":"result","duration_ms":347972,"uuid":"58a3aa71-fc9d-49c8-adf7-595d44938e3e"}
